# M2_VdP1.xps -- runs M2_VdP1.ode in one go (the steps at the top of the .ode).
#   XPPAUT 8.4:  File > Do script > M2_VdP1.xps    (or: xppaut M2_VdP1.ode -script M2_VdP1.xps)
#   XPPAUT-Web:  pick it under Scripts (group iso-test), or open the link with ?script=
speed 0.3
msg "M2, backward integration: start on the straight isochron at gamma0, integrate back by (k - th) T"
keys v 2
ans X-axis=ve|Y-axis=we|Xmin=-3.5|Ymin=-4.0|Xmax=3.5|Ymax=4.0|Xlabel=v|Ylabel=w
keys u c a
ans thc
ans c
ans 0
ans 1
keys esc
keys i 2
ans Vary1=u|Start1=-1|End1=1|Vary2=th|Start2=0|End2=0.9|Steps=80|Steps2=9|Reset storage (Y/N)=N|Use old ic's (Y/N)=Y|Cycle color (Y/N)=N|Movie(Y/N)=N|Crv(1) Array(2)=2
keys n n
msg "Window 1: each dot is the end of one backward run, coloured by its target phase th = 0, 0.1, ..., 0.9"
wait 4
keys m c
keys u c a
ans err
ans c
ans 0
ans 1
keys esc
keys v 2
ans X-axis=ve|Y-axis=we|Xmin=-3.5|Ymin=-4.0|Xmax=3.5|Ymax=4.0|Xlabel=v|Ylabel=w
keys r
keys n n
msg "Done. Window 2: every dot checked forward the M1 way; red = on its isochron. M2's limitation: more backward time gives longer isochrons but wrong dots, see M2_limitation_contraction_ML."
